 "notes": "Season rewards modal: header band (plumed helmet emblem, gold 'Season Rewards' title in Cinzel with tall S/R, burning-castle art on the right, red close button) over a body frame. A parchment band spans the top of the body: a blue crown-and-laurel banner hangs from a rod at its left and overflows the band down to y=269; 'Season 1' (Cinzel small caps, near-black ink), a thin vertical divider, 'Tier 8', the XP bar (dark track with gold fill ending at x=797, ~78% of the track interior although 750/900 is 83%), '750 / 900 XP' and a small crown crest; castle art fills the band's right end. Tier rail: a thin gold line (y 255-260) from x=279 to 1222 with small end-cap diamonds, five shield/hexagon badges numbered 7-11 (Cinzel, all one size 26; single digits were not width-fitted) and four gold diamonds midway between badges. Badge 8 is the CURRENT tier (glowing gold). Rows: FREE (silver-white label, iron-bound chest art) and PREMIUM (gold label, gold crown art) header cards with ornamental dividers above and below the label; the PREMIUM card's lower-left is covered by foreground props (rolled map, coins, lantern, chests) that also hide the body frame's bottom-left corner, so its bottom edge (y=620) is inferred from the reward cards. Reward cards per tier column: tier 7 = CLAIMED in both rows (green-tinted card and frame, green corner tab with check mark at top-right, green CLAIMED button with check icon and pale-green label); tier 8 = CLAIMABLE in both rows (glowing gold frame, warm brown fill, gold CLAIM button with dark label; this column is ~5 px narrower); tiers 9-11 = LOCKED (dark steel card, grey LOCKED button with padlock icon and grey label). Captions are cream full caps centred under the art; art rects are the measured picture bounds (they vary per item). Back to Map is a slate-blue plate at the bottom right inside the body frame, Cinzel small caps (tall B and M). Width-fitted sizes vary slightly within one style: the ten captions (fitted 18-20) are one style (~19); CLAIMED/LOCKED labels (16-17) are one style (~16-17) while the CLAIM label is visibly larger (~21)."
